# The first-party packages come from GitHub Packages, exactly as a product installs them.
@quynhonsemiconductor:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
# NO token here: pnpm 11 ignores a token in a project .npmrc on purpose (the file is committed). It goes in
# a USER-level npmrc, which works on pnpm 10 and 11; see "Authenticating to GitHub Packages" in the root README.
# Here, with a token that has read:packages:
#   ( umask 077; printf '//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=%s\n' "$TOKEN" >> ~/.npmrc )
# or, as CI does, a file outside the workspace named by NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG.
